  "investigation_notes": "**Verdict: insufficient_evidence \u2014 uploads failure root cause not proven.**\n\n**What is known:**\n\n- Both containers were `running` at check time, with very short uptimes `Up 6 seconds` and `Up 11 seconds` (E1).\n- Application `/health` returned `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2). This is a **symptom**, not a root cause.\n- App container `incidentlab-app-1` was `running:true`, `exit_code:0`, `oom_killed:false`, `restart_count:0`, user `1000:1000`, bind `source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true`, network `incidentlab_default` (E5).\n- DB container `incidentlab-db-1` was `running:true`, `exit_code:0`, `oom_killed:false`, `health:healthy`, `restart_count:0`, network `incidentlab_default` (E6). DB healthy does not prove app can connect to it.\n- Recent Docker events show `destroy/rename/start` and `kill/stop/die exit 0/destroy/rename/create/start` sequences for both containers, plus repeated successful `pg_isready` `exec_die exit 0` and `health_status: healthy` for db (E7). No non-zero `die` or OOM is recorded in the inspected state (E5)(E6)(E7).\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir:true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app 1000:1000`, `app_user_can_write:true` by owner/mode bits (E8). This argues **against** a simple owner/mode permission block, but the check itself notes it `ignores ACLs and supplementary groups` (E8), so ACL/parent-dir issues are not ruled out.\n\n**What is missing \u2014 why no cause can be claimed:**\n\n- App logs unavailable in 3 attempts (E3)(E9)(E10 includes db log attempt). Without logs, application error text for uploads, e.g. `Permission denied`, `No space left`, DB connection failure, cannot be confirmed.\n- Filesystem capacity/inode usage unavailable for `/srv/lab-data` in 2 attempts (E4)(E12) and for `/` in 1 attempt (E11). Disk-full / inode-full therefore **cannot be ruled in or out**.\n- No evidence was collected showing the cause itself for disk, permissions beyond E8, or DB dependency failure. Per task rules, a cause must not be concluded by elimination alone.\n\n**Next read-only evidence needed (after approval/repair window):** app stderr/stdout around upload request, `df -h` + `df -i` for `/srv/lab-data`, write test as UID 1000, DB connectivity from app network.\n",
